---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import DemoNav from "@components/DemoNav.astro";
import "@styles/demo.css";
---

<Base
	title="Sermon captions"
	description="Live sermon captions in Yorùbá, Igbo and Nigerian Pidgin on Noewright, a Go multi-agent runtime: Scripture is quoted from real Bibles, a hook enforces it, a judge scores every line, and the congregation follows on their phones."
>
	<div class="demo">
		<DemoNav slug="captions" position="top" />
		<section class="wrap demo-intro" data-cloud="mind">
			<p class="eyebrow"><b>Noewright</b> · Go · live demo</p>
			<h1>Sermon captions in Yorùbá, Igbo and Pidgin.</h1>
			<p class="lede" id="sc-lede">
				Speak or paste a line of a sermon. Each line runs as one Noewright graph: a clean <b>English caption</b> starts
				streaming at once while a <b>detector</b> finds any Bible passage and Go looks it up in real Bibles. Then three
				<b>translators</b> write Yorùbá, Igbo and Nigerian Pidgin captions in parallel. Run every agent on one model, or
				give each agent its own. When the preacher reads a verse aloud, a <b>scripture
				guard</b> (a Noewright hook) makes each caption quote that language's Bible word for word, and sends back any
				that doesn't. A <b>judge</b> scores every caption once it is on screen. Anyone with the follow link watches the captions arrive on
				their phone.
			</p>
			<p class="dim sc-disclaimer">
				Yorùbá, Igbo and Pidgin captions are machine translations: read the judge's scores as a second opinion, not a guarantee.
				Scripture is never machine-translated; see the Bibles below.
			</p>
			<div id="api-status"></div>
		</section>

		<section class="wrap demo-body stack" id="sc-speaker">
			<div class="panel" id="sc-wiring">
				<div class="panel-hd"><span class="label">The agents, and how Noewright wires them</span><span class="spacer"></span><span class="chip" id="mode-chip">Dry run</span></div>
				<div class="panel-bd sc-wiring">
					<div class="sc-graph" id="sc-graph"></div>
					<div class="stack sc-models">
						<div class="tabs" role="tablist" id="sc-model-mode">
							<button class="tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-mode="one">One model for all</button>
							<button class="tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-mode="per">A model per agent</button>
						</div>
						<div class="stack" id="sc-one">
							<label class="field"><span>Model</span><select class="select" id="model"></select></label>
							<label class="field"><span>API key</span><input class="input mono" id="key" type="password" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="Optional" /></label>
						</div>
						<div class="stack" id="sc-per" hidden>
							<div class="sc-agent-models" id="sc-agent-models"></div>
							<label class="field"><span>Anthropic key</span><input class="input mono" id="key-anthropic" type="password" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="For agents on Claude" /></label>
							<label class="field"><span>OpenAI key</span><input class="input mono" id="key-openai" type="password" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="For agents on GPT" /></label>
						</div>
						<label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="remember" /> Keep for this tab</label>
						<p class="dim key-note" id="key-note">Your keys go with each request, are used for that line only and are never stored. An agent with no key for its provider runs on canned output, so you can mix real and simulated agents.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="split-wide">
				<div class="stack">
					<div class="panel">
						<div class="panel-hd"><span class="label">Pulpit</span><span class="spacer"></span><span class="dim mono sc-count" id="sc-count"></span></div>
						<div class="panel-bd stack">
							<label class="field"><span>What the preacher just said</span>
								<textarea class="textarea" id="sc-text" rows="3" maxlength="400" placeholder="Proverbs 3:5 says, Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding."></textarea>
							</label>
							<div class="row">
								<button class="btn btn-primary" id="sc-send" type="button">Caption it</button>
								<button class="btn" id="sc-next" type="button">Next sample line</button>
								<button class="btn btn-ghost" id="sc-play" type="button">Play the sample sermon</button>
								<span class="dim" id="sc-status" role="status"></span>
							</div>
							<p class="dim sc-hint" id="sc-sample-hint"></p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="panel">
						<div class="panel-hd">
							<span class="label">On screen</span><span class="spacer"></span>
							<span id="sc-busy" hidden class="row" style="gap:6px"><span class="pulse"></span><span class="dim mono" style="font-size:.7rem">agents working</span></span>
						</div>
						<div class="tabs" role="tablist" id="sc-langs"></div>
						<div class="panel-bd stack">
							<div class="sc-screen" id="sc-screen" aria-live="polite"><p class="sc-screen-text dim">Captions appear here.</p></div>
							<div id="sc-verses"></div>
							<div class="sc-agents" id="sc-agents"></div>
							<div id="sc-error"></div>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="panel">
						<div class="panel-hd"><span class="label">The service so far</span><span class="spacer"></span><button class="btn btn-sm btn-ghost" id="sc-new" type="button">New service</button></div>
						<div class="panel-bd"><ol class="list-plain sc-history" id="sc-history"><li class="dim">No lines yet.</li></ol></div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<aside class="stack">
					<div class="panel">
						<div class="panel-hd"><span class="label">Follow on a phone</span></div>
						<div class="panel-bd stack">
							<p class="mid" style="font-size:.88rem">Open this link on another device and pick a language. Captions arrive as the preacher speaks, through Noewright's session events.</p>
							<input class="input mono" id="sc-follow" readonly aria-label="Follow link" />
							<div class="row"><button class="btn btn-sm" id="sc-copy" type="button">Copy link</button><a class="btn btn-sm btn-ghost" id="sc-open" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open</a></div>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="panel">
						<div class="panel-hd"><span class="label">This line, step by step</span><span class="spacer"></span><span class="chip" id="sc-cost"></span></div>
						<div class="panel-bd"><ol class="list-plain steps" id="sc-steps"><li class="dim">Agent steps appear here as they finish.</li></ol></div>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="wrap demo-body stack" id="sc-follower" hidden>
			<div class="panel">
				<div class="panel-hd"><span class="label" id="sc-f-title">Live captions</span><span class="spacer"></span><span class="chip" id="sc-f-live">connecting</span></div>
				<div class="tabs" role="tablist" id="sc-f-langs"></div>
				<div class="panel-bd stack">
					<div class="sc-screen sc-screen--follow" id="sc-f-screen" aria-live="polite"><p class="sc-screen-text dim">Waiting for the preacher.</p></div>
					<ol class="list-plain sc-feed" id="sc-f-feed"></ol>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="wrap demo-body">
			<div class="panel">
				<div class="panel-hd"><span class="label">The Bibles</span></div>
				<div class="panel-bd stack sc-bibles">
					<p class="mid">Passages read aloud are quoted from these texts, never translated by a model:</p>
					<ul class="list-plain">
						<li><b>Yorùbá:</b> Biblica® ní oore ọ̀fẹ́ láti lo Bíbélì Mímọ́ ní Èdè Yorùbá Òde-Òní, © 2009, 2017 Biblica, Inc., <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via <a href="https://ebible.org/yor/">eBible.org</a>.</li>
						<li><b>Igbo:</b> Biblica® Baịbụlụ Nsọ nʼIgbo Ndị Ugbu a nke dịrị onye ọbụla ịgụ, © 2020 Biblica, Inc., <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a>, via <a href="https://ebible.org/ibo/">eBible.org</a>.</li>
						<li><b>English and Nigerian Pidgin:</b> King James Version, public domain. The Nigerian Pidgin Bible isn't openly licensed, so Pidgin captions quote the KJV.</li>
					</ul>
					<p class="dim" style="font-size:.82rem">Biblica® is a trademark of Biblica, Inc. This demo is independent and not affiliated with Biblica or any church software company. The sample sermon was written for this page.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<DemoNav slug="captions" position="bottom" />

		<section id="feedback"></section>
	</div>
</Base>

<script>
	import "../../scripts/demo/captions.js";
</script>
